  "semantics": {
    "efficientOracle": "If n>m choose every weight1. Otherwise sort both species arrays descending and return YES if some Alice rank exceeds the corresponding Bob rank. O((n+m)log(n+m)) time, O(n+m) space, independent of k.",
    "input": "Exactly three nonempty lines: n m k; n Alice species; m Bob species. n,m1..100000,k1..1000000000; each species1..k; duplicates permitted. stdio, noninteractive.",
    "output": "One unique decision token YES/NO. Existential positive nondecreasing real species weights do not make output multiple-valid or floating. No custom checker supplied or needed.",
    "proof": "Write w1>0 and increments dt=w_t-w_(t-1)>=0. Weight difference is (n-m)w1 + sum_{t=2..k}dt*(Alice count>=t minus Bob count>=t). A positive suffix is sufficient: base1 and a single jump n+m make the difference positive. Without a positive suffix no nonnegative increment can make a positive difference. For n<=m, all descending Alice ranks <= matching Bob ranks give an injective weight-dominating pairing. A violating rank j yields threshold Alice[j] with at least j Alice fish but fewer than j Bob fish. This establishes exact equivalence and strict-equality NO."
  },
